  "findings": [
    "V7 is a continued training run initialized from v6 best48; its best source validation is at local epoch64, not epoch2. A blanket claim that later training always hurts is contradicted by this curve.",
    "Both v8 runs continue from v7 best64, preserve inherited weights, and add 4672 parameters with a zero-initialized verifier last weight. Their selected epoch2 belongs to the five-epoch head_warmup; it is not two epochs of training from scratch.",
    "V8 later joint finetuning lowers training loss eventually while failing to improve the epoch2 source-validation NMAE. This supports source-validation generalization deterioration and rare large-error instability under this schedule.",
    "The actual deployed/compared v8 checkpoint is best2, so deterioration of discarded late checkpoints cannot by itself explain its external zero-shot error.",
    "V8 best source-validation improvements over v7 are 0.44 percent and 0.42 percent relative, only 0.000262 and 0.000248 percentage points. These tiny source improvements do not establish external transfer benefits.",
    "End-of-run median source errors improve relative to epoch2, while tail and maximum errors worsen, especially for pair-preserving. The source validation degradation is concentrated in the tail rather than a uniform loss of precision."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No per-epoch external predictions or external NMAE curve were analyzed; source overfitting cannot prove that selected-checkpoint external failure is caused by overfitting rather than domain shift or source-development selection mismatch.",
    "These are single-seed histories (20262020), with 1506 validation images and 70 validation groups; causal comparisons between training stage and errors are not isolated interventions."
  ]
}
